---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FAQList from '../components/FAQList.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
import { learnToPages } from '../data/landing';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Learn-To Trips',href:'/learn-to-trips/'}];
const faqs=[
  {q:'What is a Learn-To Trip?',a:'A Learn-To Trip is travel designed around developing a skill through structured instruction and practice. The learning goal influences the destination, daily schedule, provider selection, equipment, prerequisites, and how much free time the itinerary needs.'},
  {q:'Are Learn-To Trips only for complete beginners?',a:'No. Some are designed for first-timers, while others can be structured for mixed levels or travelers progressing from existing experience. The trip page should make the expected starting level clear.'},
  {q:'Who provides the instruction?',a:'Appropriate qualified local or specialist providers deliver the technical instruction. Talon coordinates the travel and program around those providers.'},
  {q:'Can the trip include people who are not participating in the course?',a:'Often, yes. Destination and itinerary design can account for non-participants when there are meaningful alternatives and the group wants a mixed format.'},
  {q:'Does every Learn-To Trip include a certification?',a:'No. Some activities use formal certification pathways; others focus on practical instruction, progression, and supervised experience without a formal credential.'},
  {q:'Can a club use Learn-To Trips as a progression program?',a:'Yes. A community can build recurring trips around beginner entry, intermediate progression, or preparation for more advanced objectives.'}
];
const serviceSchema={'@type':'Service',name:'Learn-To Trips',description:'Skill-based group travel built around learning and progressing in activities such as scuba diving, skiing, mountaineering, wilderness skills, sailing, and surfing.',provider:{'@id':`${Astro.site}#organization`},areaServed:{'@type':'Place',name':'Worldwide'}};
const faqSchema={'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map((i)=>({'@type':'Question',name:i.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:i.a}}))};
---
<BaseLayout title="Learn-To Trips & Skill-Based Travel | Talon Expeditions" description="Skill-based group travel built around learning scuba diving, skiing, mountaineering, wilderness skills, sailing, surfing, and other activities with structured instruction and travel support." image={images.surf} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} schema={[serviceSchema,faqSchema]}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.surf}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Learn-To Trips</p><h1 class="section-title">Go somewhere worth remembering. Come home able to do something you could not do before.</h1><p>Learn-To Trips combine travel with structured instruction, practice, and progression. The destination still matters, but the itinerary is built around giving people enough time and support to actually learn.</p></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">What it is</p><h2>Travel where learning is part of the reason to go.</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>How is a Learn-To Trip different from an active vacation?</h2><p>A normal active vacation may include lessons or activities, but a Learn-To Trip is designed around skill development. Instruction, practice, equipment, provider qualifications, prerequisites, recovery, and progression are important enough to shape the destination and daily schedule.</p></div><p>The format works particularly well for groups because learning together gives travelers a common objective and a shared language. A dive club can bring new members into the sport. Friends can learn to ski together. A hiking community can develop mountaineering or wilderness capability. A social group can use sailing or surfing as the center of a warm-weather trip.</p><p>We do not treat the activity as an excuse to overfill the itinerary. Beginners need time to absorb information, recover, repeat skills, and enjoy the destination. The trip should create progress without feeling like an accelerated course squeezed between transfers.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Current and developing formats</p><h2 class="section-title">Choose the skill, then build the right setting around it.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">The deeper pages below explain how planning changes for specific skill-based trips.</p></div><div class="destination-grid">{learnToPages.map((page)=><a class="destination-card" href={`/learn-to-trips/${page.slug}/`} style={`background-image:url('${page.hero}')`}><div class="destination-content"><span class="tagline">Skill-based travel</span><h3>{page.title}</h3><p>{page.description}</p><div class="mini-tags"><span>Instruction</span><span>Progression</span><span>Travel</span></div></div></a>)}<div class="destination-card" style={`background-image:url('${images.boat}')`}><div class="destination-content"><span class="tagline">Developing format</span><h3>Learn to Sail</h3><p>Sailing-focused travel can combine onboard learning, coastal exploration, teamwork, and destination time when the right instructional provider and vessel are available.</p><div class="mini-tags"><span>Future program</span><span>Water</span></div></div></div><div class="destination-card" style={`background-image:url('${images.surf}')`}><div class="destination-content"><span class="tagline">Developing format</span><h3>Learn to Surf</h3><p>Beginner surf travel works best when instruction, beach conditions, recovery, equipment, accommodation, and the wider destination are planned together.</p><div class="mini-tags"><span>Future program</span><span>Coast</span></div></div></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="shell donor-detail"><div><div class="detail-gallery"><div class="gallery-main" style={`background-image:url('${images.water}')`}></div><div style={`background-image:url('${images.trekking}')`}></div><div style={`background-image:url('${images.fuji}')`}></div></div></div><div><p class="eyebrow">A real learning itinerary</p><h2 class="section-title">The course and the travel plan have to fit each other.</h2><p style="color:#aaa">A training provider may need specific hours, conditions, equipment, guide ratios, academic work, or recovery time. Flights, transfers, sightseeing, and social plans should be built around those requirements rather than competing with them.</p><div class="trip-facts" style="background:#171310;margin-top:28px"><h3 style="color:#fff">What changes on a Learn-To Trip</h3><div class="fact"><strong>Provider</strong><span style="color:#aaa">Qualified instruction becomes a core supplier decision.</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Schedule</strong><span style="color:#aaa">Practice, repetition, weather, and recovery need protected time.</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Equipment</strong><span style="color:#aaa">Rental, personal gear, fitting, baggage, and technical items need advance clarity.</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Prerequisites</strong><span style="color:#aaa">Fitness, medical, swimming, age, prior skills, or pre-course work may apply.</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>Progression</strong><span style="color:#aaa">The trip should have a logical path from starting level to intended outcome.</span></div></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Example trip rhythm</p><h2 class="section-title">Learning needs repetition, but the trip still needs room to breathe.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">The exact schedule varies by activity. This example shows the logic, not a fixed package.</p></div><div class="day-grid"><div class="day-card"><span class="day-label">Arrival</span><h3>Settle in & orient</h3><p>Arrival, equipment or provider check-in, local orientation, and enough rest to begin the program ready.</p></div><div class="day-card"><span class="day-label">Foundation</span><h3>Learn the basics</h3><p>Instruction, demonstration, controlled practice, and time for questions without rushing to the most advanced part of the activity.</p></div><div class="day-card"><span class="day-label">Progression</span><h3>Apply the skill</h3><p>Move into real conditions, longer sessions, or more complex tasks under the appropriate supervision.</p></div><div class="day-card"><span class="day-label">Recovery</span><h3>Rest & experience the place</h3><p>Build in lighter days, culture, food, beaches, local exploration, or other activities so the trip is not only training.</p></div><div class="day-card"><span class="day-label">Consolidation</span><h3>Repeat & build confidence</h3><p>Use additional practice to turn new information into something the participant can actually do more independently.</p></div><div class="day-card"><span class="day-label">Next step</span><h3>Leave with a progression path</h3><p>Understand what was achieved, what still needs work, and what kind of future trip or training would make sense next.</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell split-copy-image"><div><p class="eyebrow">Beginner-friendly does not mean requirement-free</p><h2 class="section-title">Good instruction starts with honest prerequisites.</h2><p class="section-copy">A beginner program can still involve medical screening, minimum fitness, swimming comfort, equipment, age limits, weather, altitude, or other conditions. Those requirements should be visible before someone commits.</p><div class="check-grid"><span>Starting experience level</span><span>Medical or activity screening</span><span>Fitness expectations</span><span>Required pre-course work</span><span>Personal and rental equipment</span><span>Insurance requirements</span><span>Certification documents</span><span>Progression and completion criteria</span></div><a class="button" href="/faq/learn-to-trips/">Read Learn-To Trip FAQs</a></div><div class="split-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.packing}')`}></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Questions before you learn</p><h2 class="section-title">The trip should answer these before departure.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Specific technical answers come from the selected instructor or provider. Talon helps make the travel and participant information coherent around them.</p></div><FAQList items={faqs} openFirst={true}/></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="Start with the skill your group wants to learn." copy="We can help determine which destination, season, instructional structure, and travel format make sense around that goal." />
</BaseLayout>
